<title>THAILAND: Thai rice vessels loading and movements at June 11.</title>
<headline>Thai rice vessels loading and movements at June 11.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry and independent surveyors detailed rice loading at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>ARCADIA	     15/05/97	     10,000	  Singapore</p>
<p>IRAN SABR	   15/05/97		9,000	  Iran</p>
<p>JULIAT		15/05/97		8,000	  Nigeria</p>
<p>XIANT YANG	  15/05/97	     10,500	  Philippines</p>
<p>BU HUNT	     15/05/97		5,500	  Vietnam</p>
<p>Sangthai Diana    16/05/97		 --	    Singapore</p>
<p>Sangthai Chenese  16/05/97		 --	    Hong Kong</p>
<p>Sangthai Radium   23/05/97		3,600	  Singapore</p>
<p>DELIGHT	     26/05/97		5,500	  India</p>
<p>SONG DHONG	  26/05/97	     13,500	  Iran</p>
<p>YI YANG	     27/05/97	    128,000	  Philippines</p>
<p>Sangthai Sunny    28/05/97		4,000	  --</p>
<p>DEBENA EXPRESS    29/05/97		7,200	  Malaysia</p>
<p>YING BAO	    30/05/97		3,750	  Singapore</p>
<p>B.U.TO 2	    02/06/97		4,000	  Singapore</p>
<p>Sangthai Ceramic  02/06/97		3,500	  Singapore</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
